cff-version: 1.2.0
title: adiungere
message: >-
  If you use this software, or the integrity specification it publishes, in research, in an expert report or
  in derivative work, please cite it using this metadata. Cite the version you depend on; where a commit
  matters more than a version, the signed commit is the identifier.
type: software

abstract: >-
  adiungere reads dashcam recordings that hold more than one camera in a single ISO base media file. It
  finds them in a library, plays either camera or both together, exports each one without re-encoding it,
  and preserves the vendor telemetry that general-purpose media pipelines discard. It publishes a per-track
  fingerprint and an integrity manifest that a third party can reproduce with ordinary tools, and it states
  plainly what those artefacts prove and what they do not.

authors:
